From a70b87e877fb1278d4ef13c99ab03c8e23fd90f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:22:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(policy): deterministic allow/escalate/deny gate for
 financial actions

Adds the action-shaped half of the policy engine alongside the existing
offer-shaped one. FinancialAction describes a payment, refund, payout or
campaign spend completely enough to judge without reading a clock or a
database, so a disputed decision can be replayed months later and come out
the same.

Nine pure rules: currency, positive amount, actor matrix, per-kind ceiling,
per-kind escalation threshold, refund-within-capture, daily cap, velocity and
geography. Every rule reports even when it passes - a record listing only
failures cannot prove the cap was checked at all.

Aggregation is deny beats escalate beats allow, written as two explicit passes
rather than a max() over an enum whose ordering a later edit could silently
reverse. A human may approve past an escalation; nobody may approve past a
denial.

Merchant policy gains two thresholds per dimension. One threshold forces a
choice between blocking legitimate large orders and waving through fraudulent
ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
