From 0cba11ef460e57db5fd2bc15f724711a6d8d3f8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:22:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(refunds): eligibility guard for money going back out

Checks the arithmetic a refund gets wrong quietly: refunding more than was
captured, forgetting to deduct earlier refunds, refunding an order that was
never paid, refunding in floats, refunding after the acquirer's window closed.
A declined card is loud; an over-refund succeeds and surfaces a month later
during reconciliation.

Decides eligibility and the ceiling, never permission - it hands the
authorization gate an action to judge rather than judging it, so a
'small refunds are fine' shortcut cannot grow into a second, weaker gate.

An order with no capture timestamp fails closed: one that cannot be aged
cannot be shown to be inside the window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M6LL3Gr7HTQxMcJnbbKLzC
