From 075c8873c224605315e1addb4d2378b5199ecab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:22:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(api): policy dry-run and authorization routes, plus
 the migration

POST /policy/evaluate answers what the gate would say without creating
anything - so a console can warn 'this needs two approvals' before the
operator commits. Limited to POLICY_EVALUATE: the response enumerates
ceilings and thresholds, which would otherwise make it a binary search for
the largest amount that slips through unattended.

POST/GET/approve on /authorizations. No request model carries merchant_id or
actor_id; both come from the verified token, which is what makes four-eyes
enforceable rather than advisory. Money is StrictInt paise throughout.

Refunds are routed through the guard first, so an ineligible refund never
becomes a pending approval sitting in somebody's queue.

The migration extends authorizations rather than adding a table - the 0001
spend-cap form and this approval-workflow form are the same object at
different stages, and splitting them means two places to look during an
incident. Adds risk_scores (with RLS) and orders.refunded_paise, the running
total the guard subtracts from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
