From 2249d378ee225f2da28e6fb7d0a9d56c7a493e8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:22:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] test: policy, risk, refunds, authorization flow and
 bypass attempts

172 new tests across five files.

The security file is written as an attacker: Phase 5's acceptance is a
negative claim - no financial action proceeds without a passing decision and
approval - and a negative claim cannot be shown by the happy path. Each test
tries to get money out and passes only when it fails: spend a pending record,
spend a denied one, spend one twice, spend a small approval on a large charge,
be both approvers, approve your own request, reach another merchant's record,
use an approval after it died.

The insider is the interesting attacker, so the fixture is a real manager at
the merchant rather than an outsider.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M6LL3Gr7HTQxMcJnbbKLzC
